\newlabel{fig:pipeline}{{2}{3}{The framework of our proposed scheme. Given a video frame $t$, we first obtain bbox proposals by an offline detection model and generate corresponding masks by an offline segmentation model. Then we classify each proposal with our motion model to construct intra-object spatial graphs, where each node is a mask proposal. During the spatial graph updating, each node aggregates mask contexts from its neighbors and updates itself to reconstruct more accurate mask. We further design a mask selection function to choose the best reconstructed mask from all nodes in graph. At last, we construct a temporal graph to retrieve historic masks of previous frames for refinement, and obtain the final result of frame $t$.}{}{}}
